  "story": "A sailor joins ropes into one long rope, two at a time. Joining two ropes costs as much as their lengths together, and the new rope can be joined again. What is the cheapest total cost? Joining 1, 1, 1 and 1 costs 8 if you join the two shortest each time (2, 2, then 4), but 9 one after another (2, 3, 4).",
